  "notes": "A Dutch progressive/electro-house producer sitting on the boundary between the two, which is what the numbers say. The kit is his entry's: \"four-square kick with a hard clap on 2&4, 16th hats, tom fills and long riser/snare builds; the progressive-house layer-accretion method across 8- and 16-bar phrases\" — so the perc lanes are tom, riser and impact (tom fills are named, unlike Guetta's or Garrix's pure riser bed), the roll ramp is authored and the sections run 16 bars. The bass is the electro-house convention the entry cites: \"buzzing sawtooth-and-distortion sidechained to the kick\", a kick mirror. The lead is \"a plucked or supersaw lead stating a simple, repeated anthem melody is the drop; loops are 8 bars\", so the melody is a low-density riff loop over 8-bar phrases and the harmony is \"archetypal and static\" `[LOW-CONF]`, a mark repeated here. Protocol Recordings is named as the institutional form of that aesthetic. ⚠ The research calls the parameters convention-derived; every velocity, density and register above is INFERRED.",
